The purpose of this directory is to test AI models to gain benchmarks to later compare with other models.

Install the local embedding evaluator used by the three scientific-quality
metrics:

```bash
uv sync --extra benchmark
```

The Anthropic benchmark preserves this branch's existing Haiku and Sonnet
result filenames. If a result already contains completed generations, the
script backfills MCTD, semantic alignment, and the GPT-4o-mini structured
rubric without regenerating those Claude answers.

```bash
uv run --extra benchmark python benchmarks/benchmarks_anthropic.py \
  --model claude-haiku-4-5

uv run --extra benchmark python benchmarks/benchmarks_anthropic.py \
  --model claude-sonnet-5
```

Set `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` for new Claude generations and `OPENAI_API_KEY` for
the shared GPT-4o-mini judge. Back up result files before the first backfill.
